@MarcoGorelli Consider this elementwise function:

```python
def f(x):
    if x is None:
        raise "bad"
    return x * 10
```

This function when applied to each element will raise if and only if there exist a null. So while

```python
def strict(s: pl.Series) -> pl.Series:
    if s.null_count():
        raise "bad"
    return s * 10
```

does contain an aggregate `null_count`, that's an implementation detail and it behaves as-if you applied elementwise `f` to each element, since the outcome is the same: query is aborted with an error.

@cmdlineluser ~~I see it's mentioned in the v1.34 release note: https://github.com/pola-rs/polars/releases/tag/py-1.34.0~~

~~So I assume the issue existed in v1.33.1 (I used previously)~~

You are correct, I'm still facing this issue in `v1.34`. Sometimes it works but sometimes it failed.
